OL,3,GNEWSAGovernment invests #71m in
OL,4,Areopening tungsten mine
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than #70m of public money will be
OL,7,Finvested into a mining company to help
OL,8,Frestart production, the chancellor has
OL,9,Fsaid.
OL,11,FThe Hemerdon tungsten and tin mine in
OL,12,FDevon will receive up to #71m from the
OL,13,FNational Wealth Fund to resume
OL,14,Foperations at the mine near Plymouth.
OL,16,FChancellor John Healey said it meant
OL,17,FBritain could tap into one of the
OL,18,Fworld's largest deposit of the mineral
OL,19,Fwhich is used in steel, electronics and
OL,20,Faerospace industries. The government
OL,21,Fsaid it would ringfence 50% of the
OL,22,Fproduction for use in Britain.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
